<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco de Montejo the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1508–<a href="/years/1565">1565</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-montejo">Francisco de Montejo</a> the Younger was a Spanish conquistador, son of the adelantado Francisco de Montejo. After his father's failed campaigns he led the decisive conquest of northern Yucatán, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a> in 1540 and Mérida in 1542 on the site of the Maya city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tho">T'ho</a>. Lords such as the Pech submitted, while the eastern provinces were subdued after a great Maya revolt in 1546–1547.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-de-montejo-the-younger.jpg" alt="Francisco de Montejo the Younger" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yodigo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monumento_a_los_Montejo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
